id: pm-context-8bbh
title: Resumable since delta packs with substantive messages and claims
description: "Add context-pack since with opaque retained-history cursors, bounded substantive comment and handoff excerpts, ranked changes and claims, strict output budget and omission receipts; measure against the core activity retry and comment-read route on a public tracker copy."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:31:40.635Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:34:07.567Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[33]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T16:32:19.146Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked: core context --for handoff is a current-state snapshot, activity digest/compact omits patch comment text, and pm-brief brief since already classifies lifecycle, priority and dependency changes but has no durable cursor, substantive comment excerpts or claim continuation. Implement only the missing resumable delta serving surface over SDK activity plus the existing certified complete item reader. Keep tracker/history semantics in the SDK. Plan non-git/no-git-PATH regressions, behavioural revert proof and public-copy three-call completeness/token comparison."
  "2026-10-21T16:39:34.156Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the since surface with SDK history replay, registered relationship ordering, content-addressed retained cursors, snapshot paging and exact whole-response byte-token ceilings. Six real-SDK regressions pass, including a built extension in a non-git tracker with an empty executable PATH, indirect unblock detection, cross-agent claims, substantive prose, deterministic retries, paginated completeness and typed retention remedies. Public-copy benchmark and unchanged full gates are running."
  "2026-10-21T16:49:29.383Z",codex-agent,"Additional strict health inspection currently fails on existing package state: pm-github expects host 2026.10.21 while the repository pins 2026.10.15, and health reports merge_fence_drift:2. Stale work and legacy provenance are advisory. Preserve the dependency pin and existing history; queue rules forbid merge-fence work. Treat health as a separate unresolved CI gate, not as evidence against since behavior. Full release gates remain mandatory and unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T16:56:23.982Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replaced only classify substantive-prose extraction with the prior omitted-text behavior, rebuilt dist, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern \"real tracker delta includes lifecycle|installed built command works\" test/since.test.ts. Exit 1: both selected regressions fail at missing comment kind/text, including the installed no-git CLI assertion. Restored the exact source and rebuilt. The eight-scenario focused run before this control passed 8/8 with native lines, branches and functions at 100 percent. Separate health follow-up: pm-context-595f remains open; no dependency or merge-fence repair performed."
  "2026-10-21T16:58:36.577Z",codex-agent,"Fair public-copy measurement complete: 1261 existing items at public commit 8ce50f94e5dcbeec5b5874dbf990c73a9e9d4b18, CLI 2026.10.21 and pinned SDK 2026.10.15. Each of two simulated sessions resumes with one call rather than three. Actual o200k_base output tokens: 496 to 371, then 540 to 373; all matching event identities and complete new substantive comments retained, no deferred rows. Reproduction and limits are documented in docs/since-benchmark.md; raw tracker artifacts remain ignored. The initial mismatched setup boundary was discarded. Source/none linked-test configuration was refused; rerunning source/schema as required by the host execution-context contract."
  "2026-10-21T17:05:49.585Z",codex-agent,"Linked execution passes: pm test pm-context-8bbh --run --progress --workspace-context source --pm-context schema --timeout 600, 8/8 tests, zero failures or skips. Initial source/none was a host configuration refusal; source/schema at the default 120 seconds timed out under concurrent host load, then passed with an explicit 600-second bound. Test-result tracking is disabled and was not changed, so this comment preserves the receipt. CLI JSON stderr also carries the typed code and next_steps via the SDK expected-error contract. Implementation is frozen; clean-HOME npm and Bun release gates remain the final verification work."
  "2026-10-21T17:16:00.727Z",codex-agent,"Final contract review found an empty-refresh edge case: content-identical state could return the input cursor. Added a deterministic checkpoint generation so every successful response advances to a distinct opaque token, while retries of the same input remain identical. Added explicit empty-refresh and retry assertions to the existing regression. Stopped only the task-owned in-flight gates and will rerun both against the corrected committed tree; earlier partial runs are not acceptance evidence. Native Bun installed-extension no-git acceptance passed 2/2 before this metadata-only cursor change."
  "2026-10-21T17:16:39.251Z",codex-agent,"Empty-refresh regression passes: the successful next cursor differs from the input even with no changes, and retrying the original cursor is byte-identical. The corrected classifier remains identical to the behavioural-revert control. Re-running the checked-in public-copy benchmark and both full release gates on the corrected source; no merge, release or item closure."
  "2026-10-21T17:20:21.819Z",codex-agent,"Added a concurrent-writer interleaving regression: another agent takes a claim after the metadata read but before the history snapshot. Own claims now come from that same SDK replay snapshot, preventing a stale own-claim reminder alongside the competing claim event. This preserves SDK-owned claim semantics and only changes the read projection. Final verification includes this ninth real-tracker scenario and the empty-refresh cursor assertion."
  "2026-10-21T17:36:38.651Z",codex-agent,"Lifecycle boundary regression reproduced a false reopen/reprioritization when a terminal item was deleted; the guard now requires a real resulting status/priority. The regression failed before the fix and passed afterward, retaining its new pre-deletion comment text. Derived unblocks also exclude closed/deleted waiting items. Delta rows now include type and status so the core digest metadata is preserved, and the benchmark oracle checks those fields. A final complete focused run and both full gates are being rerun; partial superseded runs are not counted."
  "2026-10-21T17:44:04.949Z",codex-agent,"The complete focused suite passes 10/10 at native 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Additional comment-identity control reproduced a real same-time duplicate: set comparison hid the second identical comment. Switched to multiplicity-aware comparison, preserving separate additions and suppressing already-seen copies; the new assertion failed before the fix. This changes prose selection only for duplicate objects, preserving ordinary-session output. Lifecycle, claim snapshot and cursor corrections remain covered by the same ten scenarios."
  "2026-10-21T17:52:11.015Z",codex-agent,"Final public-copy runner result after preserving core metadata: 1261-item committed public tracker, CLI 2026.10.21, two sessions, calls 3 to 1, actual o200k_base tokens 499 to 385 then 543 to 386 (22.8 and 28.9 percent lower). Full matching event identities, substantive text and type/status/title checks pass with zero deferred rows. These figures supersede the earlier narrower-output measurement. Multiplicity-aware comment regression now passes; all SDK reads invoke normal directory/item read hooks. Freeze this source for unchanged clean-HOME npm and detached same-head Bun release checks."
  "2026-10-21T18:15:29.792Z",codex-agent,"Final dependency projection now reports an item unblocked only after every prerequisite clears, and emits one actionable row when several blockers clear together. Partial removal remains blocked; later closure/deletion/reblocking ranks prior unblock rows last. The multi-edge regression also supplies complete SDK dependency metadata. Cursor retention now tolerates snapshot entries disappearing during enumeration, covered by a real missing-target filesystem case. No changes to SDK versions, history anchors or merge configuration."
  "2026-10-21T18:31:24.461Z",codex-agent,"Current complete source passes all ten focused real-tracker scenarios with native 100 percent lines, branches and functions, including the SDK history-policy preflight, partial/multiple blocker cases and vanished snapshot entries. The preflight delegates policy/read hooks to the public SDK activity API; physical reads preserve per-stream append order. Final actual-function revert control restores only addedProse from the earlier commit and must fail the same-time duplicate assertion; restore/rebuild before full gates. Call/token figures concern agent invocations and output, not internal I/O count or latency."
  "2026-10-21T18:52:44.853Z",codex-agent,Real SDK blockedBy probe confirmed that a free-text blocker leaves lifecycle status open and writes only blocked_by. Cover that supported blocker shape as well as dependency edges. Own-claim reminders must carry current blocker state so an unchanged blocked claim is not presented as actionable on the next empty refresh. This is the final read-projection correction before locked full gates; no tracker history rewrites.
  "2026-10-21T18:57:58.803Z",codex-agent,"Locked source acceptance now passes 10/10, zero failures/skips, with native lines/branches/functions all 100 percent. The supported blockedBy reason remains lifecycle-open in the SDK; it is now detected, and unchanged own-claim snapshots show blocked=true plus current bounded blocker context. Current metadata seeds items without history streams; streamed items use authoritative SDK replay. Typed refusal, no-git installed CLI, complete metadata, duplicate comments, multi-blocker readiness, competing claims, cursor advancement/expiry and bounds all pass. Freeze implementation for complete npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-21T19:14:19.018Z",codex-agent,"Installed CLI budget-header audit caught a real option-binding gap: the host exposes tokenBudget, while the new handler read only token-budget. Previous output fit the default ceiling, but a requested smaller ceiling could be ignored. Added real installed-CLI assertions for an explicit 8000 ceiling and a 512 rejection; fix both option spellings, then rerun measurements and gates. Superseded in-flight gates were stopped and are not counted as acceptance."
  "2026-10-21T19:19:29.123Z",codex-agent,"The installed command now accepts both host-normalized tokenBudget and hyphenated token-budget. Regression failed before the fix with ceiling 4000 instead of 8000 and passes after rebuilding, including typed refusal at 512. Benchmark now asserts its requested ceiling before recording results."
  "2026-10-21T19:46:12.027Z",codex-agent,"Final pinned PM-linked regression run passed all 10 real-tracker tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos: npx --no-install pm test pm-context-8bbh --run --progress --workspace-context source --pm-context schema --timeout 900. The linked command is node --test test/since.test.ts. It includes installed CLI ceilings 8000 and 512, no Git executable, unchanged original tracker bytes, typed expiry, paging, claims and same-time comments. Test-result tracking remains disabled as configured; this comment preserves the result. Full clean-identity npm and Bun release gates and the corrected public-copy benchmark remain in progress."
  "2026-10-21T19:57:59.549Z",codex-agent,"Corrected benchmark completed with actual CLI ceiling 12000 asserted in both sessions. Read-only public tracker archive at 8ce50f94e5dcbeec5b5874dbf990c73a9e9d4b18 contains 1261 items; changes stayed in its non-git scratch copy. Each session: core 3 calls versus delta 1; 1/1 matching immutable events, 0 missing, complete new comment and matching metadata, 0 deferred. Saved outputs also retain handoff classification and own-claim reminder. Exact stdout with tiktoken 0.14.0 o200k_base: session 1 core 502 versus delta 392 tokens (21.9% less), 1450 versus 1226 bytes; session 2 core 546 versus delta 392 tokens (28.2% less), 1599 versus 1228 bytes. These replace prior results affected by the option binding gap. No latency or backend transport claim. Reproduction: node test/measure-since.ts \"$PUBLIC_CHECKOUT\" 8ce50f94e5dcbeec5b5874dbf990c73a9e9d4b18; details in docs/since-benchmark.md."
  "2026-10-21T20:01:21.479Z",codex-agent,"Final feature code fa2afa2 passes both complete gates with clean HOME and Git identity: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check; same environment with bun run release:check. Each passed 354/354 tests, zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos. Native coverage reconciled all 10 required source files at 100% lines/branches/functions. c8: statements and lines 4460/4460, functions 130/130, branches 1608/1609 (99.93%), passing unchanged 99.9% branch threshold; since.ts itself is 100% in both reports. Workflow, typecheck, docstrings (38 declarations), build, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), package dry run, publish-attestation and changelog-date checks passed. Final changes after these gates are benchmark documentation and PM evidence only. Behavioral revert proofs fail for the old repeated-comment helper (1 versus 2) and old CLI budget lookup (4000 versus 8000); restored installed command passes. Local strict health remains failed for the separately recorded pm-context-595f contract warnings; no pin, history or merge repair was attempted. Runner UX observed: source/none refused, source/schema with timeout 900 passed; the default timeout was insufficient under shared load, and test-result tracking stays disabled. Cursor state is local and bounded; remote Postgres/MCP transport is not verified. Ready for a draft PR and orchestrator verification, with no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T20:43:22.567Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #164: fetched all review threads and comments (no pagination remains); three unresolved since.ts findings are under verification. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no outside-diff or nitpick sections. Branch is synchronized and already contains origin/main. Will cover compact checkpoints, indexed causal merge, exact receipt budgeting, regression revert proofs, targeted local checks, and unchanged npm/Bun release gates in CI."
  "2026-10-21T20:45:53.891Z",codex-agent,"Verified all three findings as valid: event-key snapshots breach fixed retention independent of --from; merge repeatedly sorts and shifts event streams; budgeting uses stale receipt fields. Implemented per-stream count/hash prefixes with explicit obsolete-format expiry, indexed frontier scan skipped on pending pages, incremental final receipt budgeting, and actionable capacity remedies. Whole PR review found the same receipt issue can also underfill exact-fit pages; regression covers both overflow fallback and exact fit. CI previously only installed Bun, so both unchanged npm and Bun release:check commands are now explicit CI steps."
  "2026-10-21T20:48:40.933Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs (each isolated to the changed function behavior, all other fixes retained): node --test --test-name-pattern='indexed causal merging' test/since.test.ts failed 1/1 (exit 1, four stream shifts instead of zero) after restoring the old sorting/shift merge; node --test --test-name-pattern='checkpoint size stays compact' test/since.test.ts failed 1/1 (exit 1, CURSOR_CAPACITY at 65,000 events) when fingerprint retained every event key again; node --test --test-name-pattern='receipt budgeting' test/since.test.ts failed 1/1 (exit 1, BUDGET_TOO_SMALL instead of a fitting one-row page) after reverting candidate receipt updates. Every mutation was restored immediately; no SDK histories were modified outside disposable test trackers."
  "2026-10-21T20:48:42.997Z",codex-agent,"Local results: node --test test/since.test.ts passed 15/15; targeted native coverage restricted to since.ts reports 100% lines, branches and functions. npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run docstring and git diff --check passed. pm test pm-context-8bbh --run --progress passed all three linked commands (since regressions, typecheck, docstrings), with zero timeouts. No lint script is defined. Strict local health still reports the pre-existing host-extension skew and merge fence drift tracked by pm-context-595f; dependency pins and existing history remain unchanged. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI to avoid host CPU saturation."
  "2026-10-21T20:54:26.868Z",codex-agent,"Code verification CI is green for pushed implementation 60a534e1984be670f0165a00cbb91f82968bc338: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/39673623474. Both Node 22 and Node 26 pass npm run release:check AND bun run release:check, each 359/359 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos (four full gate passes). Native coverage reconciles all 10 required sources at 100% lines/branches/functions; c8 is 100% statements/lines/functions and 99.93% branches, passing unchanged thresholds. since.ts is 100% in both coverage reports. CI tracker health, rebuilt dist consistency, workflow, typecheck, docstrings (38 declarations), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), package dry run, attestation and changelog checks passed. CodeQL also passed. Thread fixes: PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6u8N3k indexed merge and pending-page shortcut; PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6u8N3r compact stream fingerprints and capacity remedies; PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6u8N3v final receipt budgeting including exact-fit self-review case. No findings refused; latest fetched review had no outside-diff or nitpick findings. No review replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release. Next commit records this CI receipt and releases the claim only; final-head CI will be checked before handoff."
  "2026-10-22T09:33:38.205Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #164: verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6u_BtL. Recompute blockers only for graph-affecting events, retaining metadata ancestor replacements; cache membership sets during unblock classification and final supersession. Add real non-git operation-count and ancestor-replacement regressions, prove behavioral reverts, rebuild dist and run full unchanged npm/Bun gates. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-22T09:36:42.472Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs: restoring only the prior classify function makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"unrelated history\" test/since.test.ts fail 1/1 (exit 1): 13 traversals instead of 4 after graph-neutral events. Restricting the graph-path predicate to descendants and omitting metadata ancestor replacements makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"metadata ancestor\" test/since.test.ts fail 1/1 (exit 1): indirect unblock missing. Both isolated mutations restored immediately. Restored focused suite passed 17/17, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; two new regressions also passed 2/2 separately. npm ci, build and build:test pass. Existing strict health warnings remain separately tracked by pm-context-595f; no history repair, dependency bump or threshold change."
  "2026-10-22T09:50:32.733Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test run passed all 3 commands with timeout 900: since suite 17/17, typecheck and docstrings, no timeouts or failures. Added-content privacy and append-only history checks pass. Full local npm release gate remains active under shared host load; final full npm and Bun gate counts will be taken from the PR CI matrix on Node 22 and 26 before handoff. Changelog generation/check and committed dist are verified separately. No local gate failure or timeout is being claimed."
  "2026-10-22T09:55:44.082Z",codex-agent,"Review round complete for thread PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6u_BtL at code commit cb1e99d87b1f031dc19768ea91cf560bf3db9bc4. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/39758738235 passes full npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26: four gates, each 361/361, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos. Native required-source coverage passes 100% lines/branches/functions; c8 passes unchanged thresholds at 100% statements/lines/functions and 99.93% branches. Clean-checkout strict health, committed dist consistency, changelog and audit checks pass. Local focused suite passes 17/17 and linked pm tests 3/3. Local full npm run was manually stopped under host load after CI took over; no full local pass is claimed. Revert proofs are recorded above. Latest review still has no outside-diff findings, no findings refused, and whole-PR review also cached final blocker membership and covered ancestor replacements. Existing local strict health skew/fence findings remain tracked separately by pm-context-595f. No replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T19:22:32.793Z",codex-agent,"New review round for PR #164: synchronized remote head 7115b151c232320b992cd2063f0518d97b9f186a and confirmed origin/main is already contained. Sole unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSzDuFs6vLAzn is valid: Date.parse accepts loose, timezone-free and impossible calendar dates. Add strict explicit-zone timestamp validation, real non-git tracker regressions covering calendar and clock ranges, early-year preservation and inclusive offset boundaries; prove the isolated behavioral revert, rebuild committed dist and run unchanged full npm/Bun release gates. All thread comments fetched without pagination; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Earlier completed PR work remains intact."
  "2026-10-22T19:28:39.026Z",codex-agent,"Implemented strict explicit-zone ISO validation in since.ts and clarified docs/since.md. New real non-git regressions reject loose strings, missing zones, impossible days including century leap-year cases, and invalid clock/offset fields; valid Z, positive/negative offsets, fractional seconds, years 0000/0099 and inclusive millisecond boundaries pass 2/2. Revert proofs: replacing only parseFromTimestamp(options.from) with Date.parse(options.from) makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"since rejects loose\" test/since.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1, with Missing expected rejection: 1. Replacing only monthEnd.setUTCFullYear with the Date.UTC equivalent makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"since preserves early years\" test/since.test.ts fail 1/1, exit 1, because valid 0000-02-29 is rejected. Both controls were restored immediately. Whole-PR same-class review found one new --from parser; remaining timestamp comparisons use SDK history, while pre-existing usage --since intentionally supports relative values. An initial boundary assertion included the SDK workspace-init stream; corrected the fixture assertion to compare its item streams, with no parser behavior change. Run final linked tests and unchanged full release gates next."
  "2026-10-22T19:34:07.565Z",codex-agent,"Final linked pm test run passed all 3 commands using workspace-context source, pm-context schema and timeout 900: node --test test/since.test.ts passes 19/19 with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos; npm run typecheck and npm run docstring pass. npm ci, npm run build, npm run build:test, changelog generation/check, whitespace, added-content privacy and append-only history checks pass. Both behavioral controls are restored. Full unchanged npm run release:check and bun run release:check will run in the PR CI matrix on Node 22 and 26; no full local release-gate result is claimed for this round. Test-result tracking remains disabled as configured, so this comment records the linked results."
